yoyo skill show, yoyo skill install and yoyo skill init with no argument now exit 2 instead of 0. Before the fix all three exited 0 on the built binary; now they exit 2. The commit is 9b3392e7, and build, the full test suite, clippy (-D warnings) and fmt all pass.

The fix (src/commands_skill.rs, a few lines): the three missing-argument branches now return 2, the same code yoyo skill <unknown> already uses. They still print the same usage line to stderr. The REPL /skill show is unchanged, because the REPL ignores the exit code. The file is at 1983 lines, under the 2050 limit.

Tests:
• A new real-binary test in tests/integration.rs runs all three in an empty temp dir with a fake HOME and stdin from /dev/null. It checks for exit 2 and that the first stderr line is still usage: yoyo skill <sub> …. It also checks that yoyo skill list still exits 0 and that a bare init writes nothing.
• One existing unit assertion expected the old exit 0 for /skill show; I changed it to 2. No test was deleted.

Census: I took the list from every *_SUBCOMMANDS const and probed 30 of 106 members across 21 consts. I left out four consts (KNOWN, ROUTED, READ_ONLY_GIT, REGISTERED_UNDOCUMENTED) because they aren't subcommand lists for a single command.
• 74 members aren't reachable from the shell: their command isn't in KNOWN_SUBCOMMANDS. I went by the const and didn't probe them.
• 2 were skipped on purpose: skill search uses the network and lint fix calls the model.
• One other command has the same bug: yoyo config get with no key prints usage: /config get <key> and exits 0. It also shows the REPL form /config get on the shell. I filed it as #1154, with the scope in its first lines and the full table. Every other row that exits 0 takes no argument.

Docs: I added a sentence on the new exit-2 behaviour to the exit-codes paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md.
